---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SpeedTest from '../components/SpeedTest.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Internet Speed Test | PTCL Speed Test"
  description="Run a free internet speed test for your PTCL connection. Get accurate download, upload, ping and jitter results in under 30 seconds, no sign-up needed."
  canonical="/speed-test"
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Speed Test</p>
      <h1>Internet Speed Test</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Test your PTCL broadband or fibre connection. The test takes under 30 seconds and
        measures download speed, upload speed, ping and jitter against the nearest server.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 720px;">
      <SpeedTest />

      <h2>For the most accurate result</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Use an Ethernet cable</strong> if you can, Wi-Fi almost always reads
          slower than your line itself.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Close other apps and tabs</strong>, especially video streaming, downloads
          and cloud backups.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Disconnect other devices</strong> from your Wi-Fi during the test, or at
          least pause their streaming.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Run the test 2–3 times</strong> and take the middle result, single tests
          can be thrown off by a momentary dip.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Test at different times of day.</strong> Evening peak hours (7–11&nbsp;pm)
          are usually slower than mornings.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What do the numbers mean?</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Download</strong> is what your package advertises, how fast data reaches
        you. <strong>Upload</strong> is how fast you send data, which matters for video
        calls and sending files. <strong>Ping</strong> is responsiveness: under
        50&nbsp;ms is good, under 20&nbsp;ms is great. <strong>Jitter</strong> is how
        steady that ping is, under 30&nbsp;ms keeps calls and games smooth.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/guides/understanding-your-results">Read the full guide to understanding your results →</a>
      </p>

      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          <strong>Your results stay on your device.</strong> Test history is saved only in
          your own browser (localStorage), we never see it, and clearing it removes it
          completely. See our <a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
